# Upgrade Anetos

All of Anetos's modules are released together, with one version:

1. Read the upgrade guide of each minor version you move past:
   `go tool anetos docs upgrade` lists them (after the upgrade, they're
   at the new version; read the new release's notes too).
2. On the version the app has now, run `go fix ./...` first: it
   rewrites calls to names that release deprecated, and those names are
   removed in the next minor version, so `go fix` can't rewrite them
   after the upgrade.
3. Raise every Anetos module to the same version, the tool included:

   ```sh
   go get anetos.dev/anetos@vX.Y.Z anetos.dev/anetos/drivers/[[.DB]]@vX.Y.Z
   go get -tool anetos.dev/anetos/cli/cmd/anetos@vX.Y.Z
   go mod tidy
   ```

   (and any other `anetos.dev/anetos/...` module in `go.mod`: admin,
   plugins, other drivers).
4. Run `go fix ./...` again for the names the new version deprecates,
   and fix what the compiler still reports, as the upgrade guide says.
   Rename the settings, commands and process types it lists, in the
   `.env` files and the deploy files: the app refuses the old names,
   naming the new ones.
5. `go tool anetos agent:update` refreshes these agent files, and
   `go tool anetos doctor` reports settings to rename.
6. `go tool anetos check`
